  "body": "Explains the draft -> ready -> review gates in the README's Contributing section, and brings AGENTS.md and the review skill up to the rules the maintainer set on 2026-11-08.\n\n- **README.md** - new \"Draft first, then ready for review: the gates\": every PR opens as a draft; it is flagged ready on the maintainer's word or when a quick pass confirms its gates (mergeable, the author's quick gate green with pinning tests named, a complete body, the AGENTS.md laws, `.cps` exempt from the line limit); no pushes to a ready PR; the three review labels; the reviewer marker. \"Review of the maintainers' own PRs\" now describes the owner-PR review flow.\n- **AGENTS.md** - \"Every PR opens as a draft\" adds the quick-pass ready rule (user: \"the quickpass was to make em ready for review.. so flag em\"); \"Outside PRs are reviewed with /review-prs\" now covers owner PRs once ready (user: \"All PR*s made by owner should be reviewd and tagged\") and names the labels; the reviewer's \"never labels\" is corrected (it sets the review label).\n- **.claude/skills/review-prs/SKILL.md** step 1 - lists every ready PR, owner PRs included.\n\nHow tested: docs-only - read against AGENTS.md and the skill on main; an independent review (comment below) found the README ahead of AGENTS.md, fixed in the second commit. Not exercised: nothing to build or run.\n\nChangelog: none\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
